# NOTE: a `.pubignore` *replaces* `.gitignore` for the directory it sits in --
# it does not add to it. So everything the root `.gitignore` excludes has to be
# repeated here, or build output ships in the archive. (It did: one stale
# `.dill` took the tarball from 235 KB to 14 MB.)

# --- Mirrors .gitignore -----------------------------------------------------
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.build/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
.swiftpm/
migrate_working_dir/

*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/

# NOTE: no leading slash on these, deliberately. An unanchored pattern matches
# at any depth, which is the only thing keeping `example/build/` (GBs) and
# `example/.dart_tool/` (more) out of the archive. `.gitignore` anchors them
# because git only needs the root ones; "harmonising" the two files would take
# the tarball from ~170 KB to several GB and fail the publish outright.
pubspec.lock
**/doc/api/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
build/
coverage/

node_modules/
bun.lock

# Integration-test fixtures, generated by `swift tool/make_fixture.swift`.
example/assets/

# --- Published-archive only -------------------------------------------------
# Contributor documentation. User documentation lives in the monodocs repo and
# is published to monorithm.github.io/monodocs/monolens/latest/, which is what
# `documentation:` in the pubspec points at, so neither tree needs to ship.
# Excluding this also settles pub's "rename docs to doc" layout warning.
/docs/

# The redirect stub deployed to the old Pages URL. Two HTML files that exist
# only to forward browsers to monodocs; nothing for a consumer of the package.
/redirect/

# macOS-only fixture generator for the integration suite.
/tool/

# Commit tooling: commitlint and lefthook run in the repo, not for consumers.
/.github/
/package.json
/commitlint.config.cjs
/lefthook.yml
